<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<robot name="SO107_urdf">
<!--
  Edited from the CAD export (2026-09-20):
  * joint limits are the physical ranges (union of the calibrated white_left / white_right arms
    through joint_alignment, +5 deg margin) instead of +-pi placeholders. The folded rest pose sits
    past -180 deg on S2; with +-pi limits the kinematics wrapper clamped it silently and FK was
    wrong there by the overshoot.
  * link masses are set by role from so101.urdf (same printed parts and STS3215 servos, one extra
    roll servo split across L3/L4); inertia tensors are scaled with the mass; centres of mass are
    the CAD values. The export had uniform-density placeholders totalling 6.16 kg for an arm that
    weighs well under 1 kg. Used by the gravity term only; kinematics are unaffected.
-->

<material name="silver">
  <color rgba="0.700 0.700 0.700 1.000"/>
</material>

